WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:07.580
With all the chaos in Gotham City, it isn't
shocking that a few mistakes have been made

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.610
by the filmmakers who've brought the Dark
Knight to the big screen.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:16.980
So, what are some of the biggest mistakes
lurking in the Batman movies?

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.210
Caught red-handed

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:24.570
When the Joker orders his cronies to destroy
everything in Gotham's museum during Tim Burton’s

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:30.550
Batman, one henchman gleefully smacks a bunch
of red handprints all over a painting.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.149
But in the very next frame, the graffiti has
magically disappeared, and he’s back to

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:37.690
defacing a painting from earlier.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:42.500
Moms everywhere would probably like to know
where he got those washable paints.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.969
Joker’s bloody chin

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:50.289
Moments before he plummets from a helicopter,
the Joker is visibly bloody from his mouth

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:51.709
to his chin.

00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:57.250
And although the fall kills him, a close-up
shot reveals it somehow did miracles for his

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.750
beauty regimen.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.070
Selina’s rearranging kitchen

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:06.400
Single lady Selina Kyle is in such a rush
when she runs out of her apartment that she

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.550
forgets to put the milk back in the fridge.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:15.000
But when she returns after her little accident,
the carton is nowhere to be seen and the dishes

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.160
in the drying rack are moved around, too.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.150
Did her cats tidy up, or did the milk have
an even weirder night than she did?

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:25.480
That’s not the only weird thing going on
in her apartment.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:31.030
Soon after that scene, Selina starts to assemble
her Catwoman costume, brandishing a pair of

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.900
blue scissors.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.990
Or are they pink?

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.900
Maybe it’s Maybelline

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:43.470
As Batman prepares to reveal his identity
to Catwoman in Batman Returns, he's seen with

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.600
his usual dark eye makeup surrounding his
eyes.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.200
But after a quick cutaway, it's suddenly gone.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.770
This is because he's about to remove his mask,
and apparently, it was about 25 years too

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.390
early for this look.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.740
Ivy’s vanishing gloves

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:07.700
Batman and Robin from 1997 had a lot of problems,
and simple continuity was one of them.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.959
Seated in the back of a limousine driven by
Bane, Poison Ivy is clearly wearing black

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:15.590
gloves when she begins to put on a wig.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:21.709
However, in the next shot, her gloves are
gone...just another victim of Joel Schumacher’s

00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:22.799
madness.

00:02:22.799 --> 00:02:24.420
The spiked bracelets

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.110
That wasn’t the only time Poison Ivy’s
arms were the victim of bad continuity.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.879
She’s wearing thin, leaflike gloves when
she first welcomes Robin into her lair.

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:39.969
But when she angrily pushes him into her gross
swimming pool, she's suddenly wearing spiky

00:02:39.969 --> 00:02:41.430
rubber bracelets.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.249
The transporting gun

00:02:43.249 --> 00:02:48.700
In Batman Begins, Bruce Wayne is waiting at
the courthouse to shoot Joe Chill, the man

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.060
who killed his parents.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:55.290
A female assassin runs up and pushes a pistol
up against the criminal's chest instead.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:03:00.150
And when she shoots a split-second later,
she’s holding the gun at least a foot away.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.579
Not even Batman moves that fast.

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:04.769
"Where are you?!"

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:05.769
"Here."

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.310
Joker’s fast hands

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:12.930
During the iconic interrogation scene in The
Dark Knight, the Joker and Batman tangle while

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:18.760
the Gotham City Police Department looks on…
but it seems like they got a little more tangled

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.629
than anyone expected.

00:03:20.629 --> 00:03:25.810
As Batman holds Joker up against a wall, Joker
holds onto Batman’s arms with a chin-up

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:26.810
grip.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:31.489
But when the camera angle changes, the Clown
Prince is doing a pull-up instead...before

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:34.439
his hands quickly return to their first position.

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:35.499
The botched headline

00:03:35.499 --> 00:03:42.090
Gotham’s copy editors should probably get
fired for this one...or at least the props

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.090
department.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.829
In The Dark Knight Rises, Bruce Wayne stumbles
upon a newspaper headline whilst conducting

00:03:47.829 --> 00:03:53.359
some online research about the cat burglar
in town, where the word ‘heist’ is clearly

00:03:53.359 --> 00:03:54.359
misspelled.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:55.829
Guess it could have been worse.

00:03:55.829 --> 00:03:57.159
Thanks for watching!

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:01.280
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.419
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Batman movie mistakes you’ve noticed...

